= An Open Party for an Open Society

Wiosna can recruit equality movements into a party it controls, or let those
movements keep power over candidates and campaigns. Both routes grow the
social-liberal project. Only one leaves the leadership fully in charge.

Liberal bridge: **[+ spring_liberal_bridge +]/100**. Spring dissent: **[+
spring_dissent +]/100**. Movement autonomy: **[+ movement_autonomy +]/100**.

- @wiosna_open_recruit
- @wiosna_open_federate
- @wiosna_open_refuse

@wiosna_open_recruit
title: Recruit the movements into Wiosna through open primaries
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Spring and progressive strength grow; movements surrender some autonomy to the party.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Open primaries and national recruitment need one resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; spring_strength += 4; progressives_strength += 2; spring_dissent -= 7; progressives_dissent -= 5; young_support += 5; urban_progressive_support += 4; feminist_trust += 4; progressive_credibility += 4; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_left_ownership += 4; movement_autonomy -= 4; barons_dissent += 3; labor_dissent += 2; spring_liberal_bridge += 3; media_capacity += 3; news_headline = "Equality movements enter Wiosna through open primaries"

Activists gain places and votes inside the party. Wiosna gains their names,
lists and energy; independent campaigns become harder to maintain.

- #poland_card_finish

@wiosna_open_federate
title: Give movements autonomous places and campaign vetoes
subtitle: Share power rather than absorb organisations. Movement trust rises; party discipline weakens.
on-arrival: progressives_strength += 3; spring_strength += 2; spring_dissent -= 5; progressives_dissent -= 6; feminist_trust += 6; movement_autonomy += 6; young_support += 4; urban_progressive_support += 3; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_left_ownership += 4; party_unity -= 2; leadership_authority -= 2; ko_relation -= 2; psl_relation -= 3; news_headline = "Wiosna gives equality movements autonomous campaign power"

Reserved list places and a veto over rights language are written into the
agreement. The movements join because they do not have to disappear.

- #poland_card_finish

@wiosna_open_refuse
title: Keep Wiosna's candidates and message under leadership control
subtitle: Free. Preserve discipline; Spring and progressive dissent rise.
on-arrival: poland_wiosna_open_party_timer = 6; leadership_authority += 2; party_unity += 1; spring_dissent += 7; progressives_dissent += 5; feminist_trust -= 3; movement_autonomy += 2; young_support -= 2; news_headline = "Wiosna keeps equality movements outside its candidate decisions"

Movement leaders may endorse the party. They may not decide who represents
their demands inside it.

- #poland_card_finish


