= Nothing About Us Without Us

The equality-first programme attracts people who no longer accept being used
as campaign scenery. Feminist and LGBT organisations ask for a binding veto
over any retreat on the two bills.

Marriage progress: **[+ marriage_reform_progress +]/100**. Abortion progress:
**[+ abortion_reform_progress +]/100**. PSL relation: **[+ psl_relation +]/100**.

- @wiosna_veto_binding
- @wiosna_veto_council
- @wiosna_veto_refuse

@wiosna_veto_binding
title: Give the movements a binding programme veto
subtitle: Rights ownership becomes credible; coalition flexibility and leadership authority fall.
on-arrival: spring_strength += 3; progressives_strength += 3; spring_dissent -= 8; progressives_dissent -= 7; feminist_trust += 7; progressive_credibility += 5; movement_autonomy += 5; marriage_reform_progress += 4; abortion_reform_progress += 4; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_salience += 5; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_left_ownership += 5; spring_liberal_bridge += 2; leadership_authority -= 4; coalition_blur -= 3; ko_relation -= 2; psl_relation -= 6; p2050_relation -= 3; party_unity -= 2; news_headline = "Equality movements receive a binding veto over Wiosna's rights programme"

